# Line-ending policy.
#
# The default is normalisation: text files are stored with LF and checked out in
# whatever the platform wants. That is right for source, and wrong for the two
# directories below, where the *bytes* are the fixture.
* text=auto

# Byte-exact document fixtures. `fixtures.test.js` asserts that what is committed
# here equals what `build-documents.js` produces, byte for byte - and `cv.txt`
# deliberately carries CRLF line endings, because it exists to exercise the TXT
# parser's newline normalisation. Under the default policy Git strips those CRLFs
# on commit, the committed file stops being what the generator produces, and a
# fresh clone fails two tests before the reviewer has done anything wrong.
#
# `-text` disables the conversion in both directions: stored verbatim, checked
# out verbatim.
server/test/extraction/fixtures/documents/** -text

# The reviewer-facing copies of the same files, for the same reason.
samples/** -text
